# UrielSnips — Complete Claude/Codex Build Prompt Set

Yes. For **UrielSnips**, the architecture should be much smaller than Uriel Studio.

The goal is a **standalone VS Code extension containing the complete Uriel writing/snippet toolkit**, while remaining architecturally clean enough that Uriel Studio can consume the same snippet definitions later.

**Repository:**

```text
https://github.com/P1llar4/uriel-snips.git
```

**Package:**

```text
uriel-snips
```

**Extension ID:**

```text
uriel-snips
```

**Display name:**

```text
Uriel Snips
```

The prompts below are written so they can be given to either **Codex or Claude Code**.

